{"team":"NYG","col":"#5C8FF0","identity":"balanced","funnel":"run-funnel","plays_pg":62.6,"adot":7.6,"report_html":"<div class=\"report\"><h2>Matchup-Driven</h2><p>There's no bell-cow to bank on \u2014 the lead back sees just <strong>50%</strong> of carries (league ~59%), a committee that caps any one back's ceiling and makes their rushing props matchup- and script-dependent.</p><h3>The Offensive Blueprint</h3><p>In the passing game the ball funnels to <strong>Malik Nabers</strong> \u2014 <strong>29% of targets</strong> (league ~23%), a genuine alpha share that concentrates the receiving value at the top.</p><p>They run downhill \u2014 mostly inside the tackles (18% to the edge vs ~25%), a gap/power scheme that trades big plays for a steady, grinding floor.</p><p>The WR2 is unusually involved here \u2014 <strong>19%</strong> of targets (league ~15%), meaning there's bankable volume beyond the top receiver.</p><p>They lean on tempo \u2014 a 17% no-huddle rate (league ~11%) that inflates snap counts and everyone's volume.</p><p>The tight end is barely used in the passing game (11% of targets vs ~15%) \u2014 fade their TE's receiving props.</p><p>By the numbers it's a struggling unit \u2014 a 41% success rate (below the 44% average).</p><h3>In the Red Zone</h3><p>Their red-zone identity is <strong>run-first</strong> (50% pass), funnelling touchdown equity to <strong>Tyrone Tracy Jr.</strong>.</p><h2>Defense \u2014 Soft on the Ground</h2><p>They surrender <strong>142 rushing</strong> and <strong>229 passing</strong> yards per game (league ~120 / ~230). The run moves against them \u2014 <strong>target opposing RB1s</strong>.</p><p>They lock down opposing tight ends \u2014 just 26 rec yds/game (vs ~35); fade receiving props there.</p><p>They lock down opposing WR1s \u2014 just 53 rec yds/game (vs ~58); fade receiving props there.</p><p>They lock down opposing WR2s \u2014 just 32 rec yds/game (vs ~36); fade receiving props there.</p><p>They leak <strong>RB rushing TDs</strong> (0.53/game vs ~0.46) \u2014 an anytime-TD spot to attack.</p><p>Broadly a leaky unit \u2014 46% success rate allowed (vs ~44%); points come easy against them.</p><h2>The Betting Angles</h2><p>Bottom line: <strong>opposing RB1s</strong> smash on the ground and at the goal line.</p><p><em>Built on 2024\u201325 data; the profile rebuilds through the season as the current staff and roster set their own tendencies.</em></p></div>","depth":{"QB":[{"name":"Jaxson Dart","slot":"QB1","starter":true,"td":31,"props":{"Comp":19.13,"Att":29.84,"Pass Yds":202.23,"Pass TD":1.36,"INT":0.43,"Rush Yds":27.69},"d":{"completions":19.13,"attempts":29.84,"pass_yards":202.23,"pass_td":1.36,"interceptions":0.43,"rush_att":4.91,"rush_yards":27.69}}],"RB":[{"name":"Cam Skattebo","slot":"RB1","starter":true,"td":45,"props":{"Rush Att":12.51,"Rush Yds":50.78,"Tgt":4.88,"Rec":3.84,"Rec Yds":30.79},"d":{"rush_att":12.51,"rush_yards":50.78,"targets":4.88,"receptions":3.84,"rec_yards":30.79,"rec_td":0.14}},{"name":"Najee Harris","slot":"RB2","starter":true,"td":18,"props":{"Rush Att":4.06,"Rush Yds":15.95,"Tgt":3.1,"Rec":2.09,"Rec Yds":13.22},"d":{"rush_att":4.06,"rush_yards":15.95,"targets":3.1,"receptions":2.09,"rec_yards":13.22,"rec_td":0.06}},{"name":"Tyrone Tracy Jr.","slot":"RB3","starter":false,"td":28,"props":{"Rush Att":13.56,"Rush Yds":57.72,"Tgt":4.9,"Rec":3.73,"Rec Yds":28.18},"d":{"rush_att":13.56,"rush_yards":57.72,"targets":4.9,"receptions":3.73,"rec_yards":28.18,"rec_td":0.11}},{"name":"Devin Singletary","slot":"RB4","starter":false,"td":23,"props":{"Rush Att":5.19,"Rush Yds":21.96,"Tgt":3.1,"Rec":2.12,"Rec Yds":13.54},"d":{"rush_att":5.19,"rush_yards":21.96,"targets":3.1,"receptions":2.12,"rec_yards":13.54,"rec_td":0.03}}],"WR":[{"name":"Malik Nabers","slot":"WR1","starter":true,"td":27,"props":{"Tgt":10.15,"Rec":6.48,"Rec Yds":76.05,"Rec TD":0.33},"d":{"targets":10.15,"receptions":6.48,"rec_yards":76.05,"rec_td":0.33}},{"name":"Malachi Fields","slot":"WR2","starter":true,"td